# Read directly by the application (hosted/src/db/client.ts, hosted/drizzle.config.ts).
# Hosted uses its own dedicated MySQL database, separate from the root
# application's database (matching the dedicated-database isolation already
# used for web.sameview.app in production).
#
# Local development may reuse the already-running root compose.yaml MySQL
# server as the MySQL server, pointed at a separate local database
# (sameview_hosted) created once alongside it — not the root sameview
# database. This file is not itself read by compose.yaml.
#
# In production this must be provided as a real environment variable / a
# server-side ".env" file for the Hosted application — never committed,
# never uploaded by CI. The production database name/credentials are
# provisioned separately once a dedicated Hosted database exists in Plesk.
DATABASE_URL=mysql://sameview:sameview@localhost:3306/sameview_hosted
